{
  "description": "Shared cases for the RAG configuration equality contract. Each case gives two values a and b, the ignored_keys collection, and whether configs_equal(a, b, ignored_keys) must be true. The backend (DashAI/back/services/RAG/config_equality.py) and the frontend (DashAI/front, mirrored implementation) both read this file, so the cases use only plain JSON values: null, booleans, numbers, strings, arrays and objects with string keys. Values that JSON cannot express (tuples, sets, bytes, NaN, Infinity, custom objects, non-string keys) are tested in the backend only. Numbers beyond the safe range are outside the contract: any number, integer or float, whose value is integral and whose absolute value exceeds 2**53 - 1 is malformed and both the backend and the frontend raise an error for it. Non-integral floats (for example 0.5 or 1e-9) and integral values within the bound are ordinary numbers. The top-level malformed_cases list holds entries of the form {name, a, b, ignored_keys}; each pair must make the comparison raise an error in both argument orders, and no equality expectation is given for them. Object keys are plain strings, so a key named __proto__ is an ordinary key. Strings compare by Unicode code point with no normalization. Equality rules: objects are equal when, after dropping the ignored keys at every object level, they have exactly the same keys and equal values, in any key order; arrays are equal when they have the same length and equal elements in order; booleans never equal numbers; null never equals an absent key; numbers compare by value (1 equals 1.0); strings never equal numbers.",
